 3. Retail Billing with Discount Rules
1. Problem Statement
Develop an itemized retail bill for multiple products. Apply a discount when the pre-tax subtotal reaches a threshold, limit the discount to a maximum concession, and calculate tax on the discounted amount.
2. Objectives
•	Calculate line totals and subtotal.
•	Apply threshold-based discount with a cap.
•	Calculate tax and final invoice amount.
3. Assumptions
•	The example uses three products with quantity and unit price.
•	A 10% discount applies when subtotal is at least ₹1,000; maximum discount is ₹150.
•	Tax is 5% of the subtotal after discount.
4. Algorithm
1. Store product names, prices, and quantities in a list.
2. Calculate each line total and subtotal.
3. Apply discount condition and maximum cap.
4. Calculate tax and final total.
5. Print the itemized invoice.
5. Flowchart
 
