 6. Warehouse Inventory Reconciliation
1. Problem Statement
Compare opening stock, received stock, dispatched stock, and physically counted closing stock for several products. Detect discrepancies and calculate replenishment needed to reach a target stock.
2. Objectives
•	Calculate expected closing stock.
•	Compare expected and physical stock.
•	Calculate discrepancies and target replenishment.
3. Assumptions
•	Expected stock = opening + received − dispatched.
•	A negative expected stock is invalid.
•	Target stock is 20 units for each product.
•	Discrepancy = physical closing − expected closing.
4. Algorithm
1. Store each product record as a tuple.
2. Calculate expected closing quantity.
3. Compare with physical closing quantity.
4. Calculate replenishment to target if stock is below target.
5. Display reconciliation results.
