 10. Food Waste Monitoring System
1. Problem Statement
Compare meals prepared, meals served, and leftovers over several days. Calculate waste percentages and identify days where waste exceeds an acceptable threshold.
2. Objectives
•	Calculate leftover meals and waste percentage.
•	Compare daily waste against a threshold.
•	Summarize total waste over the period.
3. Assumptions
•	Meals prepared and served are non-negative integers.
•	Leftovers = prepared − served.
•	Waste percentage = leftovers / prepared × 100.
•	A day is flagged if waste percentage exceeds 10%; prepared meals must be greater than zero.
4. Algorithm
1. Store daily prepared and served counts in a list of tuples.
2. Calculate leftovers and percentage for each day.
3. Flag waste percentages above 10%.
4. Sum total prepared, served, and leftover meals.
5. Print daily and overall results.
5. Flowchart
 
6. Pseudocode
BEGIN
INPUT venue, equipment, catering, transport and certificate costs
INPUT sponsorship and participant contribution
CALCULATE total cost
CALCULATE shortfall after sponsorship
CALCULATE minimum participants needed
DISPLAY total cost and shortfall
END
7. Python Source Code
v = float(input("Venue cost: "))
e = float(input("Equipment cost: "))
c = float(input("Catering cost: "))
t = float(input("Transport cost: "))
s = float(input("Sponsorship: "))
fee = float(input("Contribution per participant: "))
total = v + e + c + t
shortfall = max(0, total - s)
print("Total Cost:", total)
print("Shortfall:", shortfall)
print("Participants Needed:", int(shortfall / fee) + (shortfall % fee > 0))
